<<
/Title (Low-code platforms allow applications to be developed mainly through visual tools instead of large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled from predefined components such as forms, reports and dashboards, and behaviour is defined through workflows, rules and configuration, with a small amount of scripting for specific needs. This reduces development time and effort and lets a wider range of people take part in building business applications.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 465 0 R
/Next 525 0 R
>>
